sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): stage 6 of the command development pipeline. Each task VM host keeps one stopped base VM that never gets an identity; its ZFS snapshot is the base a task start copies. After a release, and once a day, every host starts its base VM, converges it as a task start would, stops it and snapshots it; the snapshot is proven with one task start and the Gateway promotes it. There is no Incus image and no publish. Nothing is copied between hosts. The per-host run: docs/cli/task/vm-image-refresh.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 6 · per-host task image and seed refresh
  %% kind: pipeline.6-task-image-seed-refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=each host tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=base VM tone=gray
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>one run per host
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Base VM<br/>shark-base
  Note over GW: Start the refresh<br/>release · daily
  %%> Triggers:
  %%> - every Gateway release, as soon as Swamp has loaded its commit and while the release switches (the release's step "Admit VM refreshes"); a code-only release refreshes too, because the base holds the warm checkout and the nested Gateway agent of the commit
  %%> - a daily Schedule; it only dispatches the admission
  %%> - a host with a refresh open keeps it, and the newest commit waits behind it; the run that ends admits that commit
  GW->>SW: Start one run per host<br/>all in parallel
  %%> Why:
  %%> - each host bakes its own image and seed; copying them between hosts is not a supported flow
  loop each task VM host, in parallel
    SW->>H: Log egress<br/>host bridge, log only
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - sets up the egress log of the host bridge: an nftables rule, an rsyslog file and the DNS log of the bridge's dnsmasq; nothing is blocked
    %%> - the first run sets `raw.dnsmasq`, which runs the setup of the bridge again and restarts its dnsmasq: running VMs lose DNS for about a second, and Incus runs that dnsmasq without its AppArmor profile
    SW->>H: Start the base VM<br/>incus start
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a new host has no base VM yet: it is made here, once, from the stock Ubuntu VM image and an empty seed volume, and the converge that follows builds everything else
    SW->>VM: Converge<br/>the same converge as a task start
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - outer VM: packages, tools, Swamp, orbit-agent, the Pi server, sshd and UFW at the release's pins; each part runs only when its digest changed
    %%> - the warm checkout: main at the release commit, installs only where a lock file changed
    %%> - each container: migrations and restarts only when the code changed; no wait for nested services and no identity wipe
    %%> - a base VM without a nested fleet builds it once, in the same converge: the containers from stock Ubuntu, the nested Gateway from one local `gateway-bootstrap` run, app-dev and app-prod through its own Orbit, and a Doctor wait; a base VM with its fleet skips the build
    SW->>H: Stop and snapshot<br/>VM and seed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops the base VM and snapshots it and its seed volume; ZFS snapshots, about 1 s
    SW->>H: Prove the candidate<br/>one task start
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - steps 2 to 4 of a task start from the new snapshot with a free slot identity, then its release
    SW->>H: Prune old snapshots<br/>keep -previous
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - keeps the new snapshot and the one before it; removes older ones
    SW->>H: Remove host leftovers<br/>after a refresh that passed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes images, seed volumes and projects no current path makes
    %%> - a failure fails no refresh; the result says `host_clean: succeeded`, `failed` or `skipped` (the refresh failed first)
  end
  alt every host refreshed
    SW-->>GW: Host refreshed<br/>terminal event per host
    Note over GW: Promote the snapshot<br/>task starts copy it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - target about 25 s per host for a no-op refresh before the proof; one slow host does not hold the others
    %%> - the first refresh of a new host builds the whole base, its nested fleet included (about 30 min of it)
  else a refresh failed
    SW--xGW: Host not refreshed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Alert · try again<br/>next trigger
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the base VM is rolled back to the recorded snapshot and the run's snapshot removed; the identity that proved it is released
  end
